A||N||13||Bob Englert||NC Fiero meeting March 10th||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||02-21-2001||08:59 AM||||Thanks very much to everyone who attended the Feb 3rd meeting in Cary.  We<BR>had about 25 people and about 13 Fieros in attendance.  Ed and Rosy Parks<BR>stopped by during their trip to deliver and pick up a Fiero for Bert in<BR>Wilson.  It was great to see all the cars, including Bert's 'new' 3.4<BR>conversion that Ed had just delivered and the 3800 race Fiero that came on a<BR>trailer.  5 of us met at the I-40 rest area between Burlington and<BR>Greensboro and drove over to Cary together.  I love seeing a line of Fieros<BR>traveling together...  We had Fieros from Greenville, Wilson, Jacksonville,<BR>Raleigh, Chapel Hill, Greensboro, King, and Hickory.<P>FieroLisa has set up a nice web site for our very informal<BR>Fiero group.  The Tarheel Fiero web site currently has pictures of the Feb<BR>meeting and we hope to include more information and pictures in the future.<BR>If you have any good pictures of your Fiero or a web site that you would<BR>like to share please email Lisa at FieroLisa@aol.com .  She would be happy<BR>to add them to the site. Check it out at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/</A> <BR>and tell us what you think.<P>Our next meeting is scheduled for March 10th at 1:00PM  in the Hickory NC<BR>area.  Jack Cooke has made arrangements for us to meet at the Golden Corral<BR>steakhouse just off I-40 at exit 125.  Turn right at the top of the ramp, GC<BR>will be about 1/2 mile on the right.   Hope to see some of the western NC<BR>Fiero owners at the next meeting.  Depending on the weather, maybe we can<BR>take a short run into the hills after our lunch.  Any ideas?<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
